; fas9_assoc_manager.scr - facit script of step 9.15 for the persistent subentity managers' history entries (F9.11: the
; "extra or removed edge, face or vertex before and after" pairs that step 9.10 could not make). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_assoc_manager.scr
; It starts from AutoCAD's own acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has none).
; SOLIDHIST 1 makes every solid keep its history and the drawing's persistent subentity manager (ACDBASSOCPERSSUBENTMANAGER from
; 2013, ACDBPERSSUBENTMANAGER before) a history entry for every step: the drawing is built one operation at a time and saved after
; each (`;SAVE history <operation>`), so the entries one operation adds are the difference of two consecutive files. The core picks
; edges with a typed point in an isometric view (the same pick as a click), which is what FILLETEDGE and CHAMFEREDGE need.
;
; Operations, in the order they are made: BOX, CYLINDER, SPHERE, CONE, WEDGE, TORUS, PYRAMID; FILLETEDGE of one edge of the box,
; of a second edge, CHAMFEREDGE of the cylinder's circle; UNION, SUBTRACT and INTERSECT of two solids each; EXTRUDE, REVOLVE
; and SWEEP of a closed profile into a solid; SLICE.
